    fn blame_color_index_corrected(&mut self,commit:&str)->usize{
        if let Some(v)=self.blame_commit_colors.get(commit) {
            // If map was polluted by earlier or_insert 0 for a newly seen commit in this same call, we can't distinguish. Maintain a separate order encoded in grep_file? Instead: this function is called after an or_insert in emit_blame_line; for the first distinct commit it's correct (0), for later distinct commits the earlier code inserted 0 too. To fix, we track distinct order via blame_prev_commit and a counter stored in map values: if this commit's stored value was just inserted in this call, caller set is_new_block based on prev commit, not map. Hmm.
